TEXT -96 -200 Left 3 ;#55 Series LC circuit frequency sweep
TEXT -96 -144 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hqhV50852jA
TEXT -96 -104 Left 2 ;An AC sweep from 5 kHz to 200 kHz of the same series circuit and generator.
TEXT -96 -72 Left 2 ;The stack voltage and impedance dip to a minimum at resonance; below it the circuit is capacitive, above it inductive.
TEXT 480 16 Left 2 ;CH1: voltage across the whole C1 + L1 stack (Alan's channel 1).  CH2: voltage across L1 (channel 2).
TEXT 480 48 Left 2 ;V(C1) = CH1 - CH2, the scope math trace.  V1: 4 V p-p open circuit, Rser = 50 ohm generator output.
TEXT 480 80 Left 2 ;Assumed (not stated in the video): L1 = 220 uH with 1 ohm winding resistance, C1 = 100 nF, so f0 = 33.9 kHz.
TEXT 480 160 Left 2 !.ac dec 200 5k 200k
TEXT 480 200 Left 2 !.meas ac F_RES WHEN im(V(ch1)/I(C1))=0
TEXT 480 240 Left 2 !.meas ac Z_RES FIND mag(V(ch1)/I(C1)) WHEN im(V(ch1)/I(C1))=0
TEXT 480 280 Left 2 !.meas ac STACK_RES FIND mag(V(ch1)) WHEN im(V(ch1)/I(C1))=0
